				How do I register to vote?




				 You must be 18 years old and a U.S. citizen. You can register in person, by mail or at the Registry of Motor Vehicles. You will receive verification by mail after registering. The annual census is mailed every January 1, if you do not answer it your voting status will be marked inactive and you will not be listed on the active voting list. If you move within town or change your name, you must re-register with the new information. A mail-in voter registration form will be sent to you if requested. You must register to vote at least 20 days prior to any election. Please visit the Secretary of the Commonwealth’s election website for more voting information or call toll free 1-800-462-VOTE. 

						 Secretary of the Commonwealth 

				 Town Clerk 











				Where and When is the annual town meeting and election?




				 The annual town meeting is held on the first Monday in May. The annual town election is held on the third Saturday in May. All meetings and elections are held at the Town Hall. 
				 Town Clerk 











				Where do I vote?




				 All Whitman voters cast their ballots at the Town Hall, 54 South Avenue, Whitman, Massachusetts, 02382. 
				 Town Clerk 











				How do I obtain a birth, marriage, or death certificate?




				 Vital records are on file in the community where the event occurred and also in the community where residency was listed on the day of the event. Whitman’s vital records are from 1875 to the present time. Certified long form copies are $5 each. They can be requested over the counter or by mailing a $5 check made out to the Town of Whitman, please enclose a self addressed stamped envelope to: 
Town Clerk
P.O. Box 426
Whitman, MA 02382 
You can now order birth, death, and marriage certificates online by visiting the  

						 Online Payments Center. 

				 Town Clerk 











				How do I license my dog?




				 The licensing period is July 1 - June 30 each year. A proof of rabies certificate must be presented and proof of neuter or spay must be shown. The cost of licensing is: Female / Male - $15 Spay / Neuter - $10 Senior rate (over 70) is free A late fee of $25 is imposed on any license issued after August 31. A rabies clinic is held every year, call the Board of Health for date at 781-618-9755. 
				 Town Clerk 











				How do I apply for a marriage license?




				 Both parties must apply together. There is a three day waiting period after you file your intention. The cost to file is $30. You cannot apply more than 60 days prior to the marriage. 
				 Town Clerk 











				How do I get a business certificate (DBA)?




				 Business certificates are $40 for four years. You and any co-owners must appear in person in the office to sign the business certificate. If any changes occur within the four years, or you discontinue the business, you and any co-owners must come in and file the change for a fee of $10.

				 Town Clerk 











				How do I get a fishing or sporting license?




				 For more information or to obtain a fishing or sporting license please visit the  


						 Massachusetts Department of Fish and Game. 

				 Town Clerk 











				How can I get help with food, rent, or fuel assistance?




				 The Whitman Food Pantry number is 781-447-8560. Rent, utilities, and fuel assistance is handled through the Council on Aging at 781-447-7619. 
				 Town Clerk 











				I have a large item for trash. Who should I call?




				 Call Waste Management at 800-972-4545 to schedule a pick-up. 
				 Town Clerk 











				How can I find out what sports leagues and recreational activities are in Whitman?




				 Call the Recreation Department at 781-618-9758. 
				 Town Clerk 











				I have a problem with a landlord / tenant. Who should I call?




				 Contact the Office of the Attorney General at 617-727-2200 or visit the website. 

						 Attorney General&#39s Guide to Landlord/Tenant Rights 

				 Town Clerk 














